{{en-adj|-}}

# Standing [[elevated]], on or as if on the [[tip]]s of one's [[toe]]s.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Romeo and Juliet|III|v|passage=Night's candles are burnt out, and jocund day / Stands '''tiptoe''' on the misty mountain tops.}}
#* {{RQ:Tolkien Return of the King|Minas Tirith|39|And ever as they talked Beregond was more amazed, and looked with greater wonder at the hobbit, swinging his short legs as he sat on the seat, or standing '''tiptoe''' upon it to peer over the sill at the lands below.}}
