===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To walk quietly with only the [[tip]]s of the [[toe]]s touching the ground. {{defdate|from late 14th C.}}
#* {{RQ:Twain Huckleberry Finn|chapter=II|page=8|passage={{smallcaps|We}} went '''tip-toeing''' along a path amongst the trees back towards the end of the widow's garden, stooping down so as the branches wouldn't scrape our heads.}}
#* {{RQ:Lincoln Pratt's Patients|chapter=13|passage=We '''tiptoed''' into the house, up the stairs and along the hall into the room where the Professor had been spending so much of his time.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|lyricist=w:Al Dubin|composer=[[w:Joe Burke (composer)|Joe Burke]]|artist=w:Nick Lucas|title=w:Tiptoe Through the Tulips|year=1929|passage='''Tiptoe''' through the window / By the window, that is where I'll be / Come '''tiptoe''' through the tulips with me / '''Tiptoe''' from your pillow / To the shadow of the willow tree / And '''tiptoe''' through the tulips with me.}}

